          "settings": {
            "title": "How do I clean a silicone bib?",
            "answer": "<p>Three options: wipe clean under the tap after meals, run it through the dishwasher on the top rack, or drop it in with the regular dish load. Avoid high heat drying over long periods — top rack dishwasher is fine, but the heating element at the bottom of the machine will degrade silicone faster over time. The single molded construction means no seams or crevices for food or bacteria to hide in.</p>"
          }
